'''Toepick''' is the [[Omnitrix]]'s DNA sample of an [[Toepick's Species|unknown species]] from an unknown planet.

==Appearance==
Toepick is a greenish yellow-skinned, ogre-like alien with long and misshapen arms that have weed-like spikes coming out of them, pointy fingertips, and a visible belly button. He wears a simple pair of black briefs with a metal dark green waistline with white bolts on it. His eyes are glowing green and can be seen through the bars of a dark green metal cage helmet worn on his head. Inside his helmet is Toepick's terrifying face, which is supposed to resemble an eldritch horror.{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick's Face Eldritch Horror.PNG]]|group = DJW}} He also has a layer of tentacles that covers his true face.{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Face Tentacles.png]]|group = DJW|name = tentacles}} In addition, he has a type of layered multiphasic eyesight that makes his already mediocre vision even worse when looking at multidimensional or unknowable sights.{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Cannot Frighten Himself.png]]|group = DJW|name=vision}}

Toepick's helmet has two horns protruding from the sides of it, and also a crest that resembles a toenail in shape. The cage's door has five bars, three of which are in the center of the door. It opens in two halves, with the lock in the very center of the door, staying on the right half. Connected to this cage is Toepick's armor, which wraps around his shoulders and goes halfway down his chest, and is connected to his briefs by chains. When Toepick's helmet prepares to open, it releases a small amount of green gases as it depressurizes.{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick's helmet depressurizes.png]]|group = DJW}} It is also incredibly difficult to damage.{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick's Helmet.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

Toepick's [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]] symbol is on the helmet's extension covering his chest, with two green metallic protrusions accompanying the symbol on both sides.

==Powers and Abilities==
[[File:SD (574).png|thumb|Nightmarish Face]]
Toepick's only known way of defeating his enemies is with his extremely scary face, which taps into the  fears locked in all beings' subconscious and primitive brains.{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick's Face Primordial Fears.PNG]]|group = DJW}} Toepick's face is so hideously horrifying that almost no being in the known universe can look at it without being scared to the point of turning pale white. It can also induce sickness and nausea, as shown when [[Argit]] vomited several things he had eaten after seeing it.<ref name="CIU"/> If someone were to take a photograph of Toepick's face, the picture would come out blurry, but it would still make people uneasy.{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick's face in a photograph.png]]|group = DJW}}

The sight of Toepick's face can cause adverse effects on almost every being in the [[Universe (Classic)|universe]],{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Adverse Effects.png]]|group = DJW}} even a [[Celestialsapien (Classic)|Celestialsapien]]'s personalities.{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Can Scare Celestialsapien Personalities.png]]|group = DJW}} The most common of these effects are the inducement of terror and insanity, as a [[Dwarf Star]]-powered [[Psyphon]] was so terrified by Toepick's face that he begged him to stay away in-between screams of terror.<ref name="SD">''[[Special Delivery]]''</ref>

Toepick has a degree of enhanced strength, enough to lift a car.{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Enhanced Strength.PNG]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Can Lift a Car.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

Toepick's multiphasic eyesight specifically blocks him from perceiving sights that are multidimensional or unknowable, allowing him to gaze at himself or other incomprehensible horrors, including other members of his species, without being frightened.{{Refn|group = DJW|name=vision}}

==Weaknesses==
There are certain beings Toepick is unable to scare, such as [[Ma Vreedle]] because "she [has] seen worse"{{Refn|[[:File:Ma Vreedle Not Scared of Toepick.PNG]]|group = DJW}}, [[Dagon]],{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Cannot Scare Dagon.png]]|group = DJW}} and [[Professor Paradox]], who can see Toepick's face clearly, as it is not an unknowable horror to him, therefore he is able to overcome his initial fears.{{Refn|[[:File:Paradox Can See Toepick's Face.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

Toepick's vision is considered worse than mediocre, making it difficult for him to see.{{Refn|group = DJW|name=vision}} 

==History==
===Omniverse===
*Toepick first appeared in ''[[Special Delivery]]'', where he scared and defeated a [[Dwarf Star]]-powered [[Psyphon]].{{Refn|Despite first appearing in ''[[Special Delivery]]'', Toepick was never locked in the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]].{{Refn|[[:File:New Aliens in OV Weren't Locked.png]]|group = DJW}} This is supported by Ben already knowing how to utilize Toepick's abilities.<ref name="SD" />|group = note}}
*In ''[[Something Zombozo This Way Comes]]'', Toepick scared [[Zombozo (Classic)|Zombozo]] into destroying his own machine, despite being scared of Zombozo himself, thus turning all the [[Zombie Clowns|zombie clowns]] back to normal.
*In ''[[Cough It Up]]'', Toepick scared Psyphon and [[Argit]] in order to get the dehydrated [[Dehydrated Techadon Army Cube|Techadon Army Cube]] out of the latter's stomach.
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Toepick appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Original Future Timeline]]===
*In ''[[Ken 10]]'', Toepick was mentioned by [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] as one of [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken]]'s aliens in the latter's [[Omnitrix (Ken's Replica)|Omnitrix]]. At Ken's request, his father replaced Toepick with [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]].

