==Trivia==
[[File:Toepick_Face_Model.png|thumb|Toepick's tentacle face]]
*[[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken]] finds Toepick's face to be so gross that he did not want to turn into him when he received his own [[Omnitrix (Ken's Replica)|Omnitrix]].<ref name="Ken 10">''[[Ken 10]]''</ref>
*Toepick is [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s scariest alien{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick is Ben's Scariest Alien.png]]|group = DJW}} and his second least favorite alien; his least favorite overall being [[The Worst]].{{Refn|[[:File:Ben's Least Favorite Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Toepick was first mentioned in ''[[Ken 10]]''; at the time, there were never any plans to design him during the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' as characters without screen time would be an undesirable financial expense to the studio.{{Refn|[[:File:No Plans To Design Atomix and Toepick in OS.png]]|group = TNP}}
**Incorporating Toepick into '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''' and giving him a physical form and powers was [[Derrick J. Wyatt]]'s idea.{{Refn|[[:File:DJW Thought of Atomix and Toepick.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
**Toepick's appearance was inspired by an artpiece from the [[Wikipedia:Autry Museum of the American West|Autry Museum]]{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Artpiece Inspiration.png]]|group = DJW}} while his powers were inspired by the works of [[Wikipedia:H.P. Lovecraft|H.P. Lovecraft]].{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Inspiration.PNG]]|group = DJW}} Had [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]] designed him when his name was first conceptualized, he would likely look different.{{Refn|[[:File:OS Atomix and Toepick Would Look Different.png]]|group = TNP}}
*Derrick designed Toepick's tentacle face for Bandai, which was used for his deluxe figure and mini-figure.
*From Arc 4 of '''Omniverse''' onwards, Toepick replaces [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]] in the opening intro of the show, particularly in the part where the latter initially appeared alongside [[Shocksquatch]], [[Bloxx]], and [[Crashhopper]].
*Toepick's action figure's voice box allows you to hear him say "You can pick your friends, you can pick your toes, but you can't pick your friend's toes." This is a play on the phrase "You can pick your friends, you can pick your nose, but you can't pick your friend's nose".
*Despite having a layer of tentacles covering his face, Toepick cannot use his tentacles to attack blind beings.{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Cannot Use Face Tentacles.png]]|group = DJW}}
*The enhanced version of ''Ken 10'' featured pop-up trivia telling the viewer that they "don't even want to know about Toepick".{{Refn|[[:File:Ken 10 Pop-up (8).png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="Ken 10">''[[Ken 10]]''</ref>
*[[Benzarro]]'s version of Toepick is not scarier than his other counterparts.{{Refn|[[:File:Benzarro Toepick.png]]|group = DJW}}
*A hypothetical [[Ultimate Forms|Ultimate]] version of Toepick would have the power to radiate fear.{{Refn|[[:File:Ultimate Toepick Power.png]]|group = DJW}}
*[[Ben 23]]'s transformation of this species, Fright Face,{{Refn|[[:File:Fright Face Proof.png]]|group = DJW|name = Ask.fm}} was revealed by Derrick after the series ended. He declined to specify whether it was conceived during or after production.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben 23 Alien Names Revealed After Production.png]]|group = DJW}} Thus, the wiki considers it non-canon and unofficial.
**Fright Face polled so low that he was only used once.{{Refn|group = DJW|name = Ask.fm}}{{Refn|[[:File:Ben 23 Doesn't Use Toepick.png]]|group = DJW|name = image}}
*When the cage on Toepick's head opens, sounds of terrified screams, agonized wailing, roaring, unholy groans and wails, hissing, and deep demonic laughter can be heard until the cage is once again closed or when Toepick turns into another alien.

